  Hmm, teleport in and of itself is one of the biggest pains in the butt
that the game has to offer; its rarely deadly (I'm reeeeeal careful in
shops if there's a chance I might get zapped out), but it can just be
intensely annoying trying to get from one side of the level to the other
nineteen different times, because it keeps zapping you back from whence
you came.  This is much worse when trying to tunnel, as the extra time =
that much more chance you'll teleport.  In fact, the only use I've found
for random teleport is that its an easy way to get shopkeepers mad at me
once I'm powerful enough to kill them off.
  Teleport control would seem to be more useful, but I've only had it a
couple of times, and haven't had a chance to play with it thoroughly
enough to reach a verdict.

  Incidentally, time for my latest death rant.  Babydoll, the 16th level
